From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivo Nunes <ivo@nunes.uk>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:00:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libdatachannel: include <algorithm> for std::transform

configuration.cpp uses std::transform without including <algorithm>.
It used to arrive through other standard headers, but Godot builds with
_LIBCPP_REMOVE_TRANSITIVE_INCLUDES, so with Apple's libc++ the file
doesn't compile ("no member named 'transform' in namespace 'std'").

Test: build Purr's macOS editor.

Upstream: backport of libdatachannel commit 69bee9a ("Fix build with
libcxx 20.1.8"),
https://github.com/paullouisageneau/libdatachannel/commit/69bee9a719bccd151a67d2582f7be4abc0c29612
Drop this patch once a libdatachannel release includes it.
---
 .../thirdparty/libdatachannel/src/configuration.cpp              | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/modules/webrtc_native/thirdparty/libdatachannel/src/configuration.cpp b/modules/webrtc_native/thirdparty/libdatachannel/src/configuration.cpp
index fe28aef7..897be5ea 100644
--- a/modules/webrtc_native/thirdparty/libdatachannel/src/configuration.cpp
+++ b/modules/webrtc_native/thirdparty/libdatachannel/src/configuration.cpp
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 
 #include "impl/utils.hpp"
 
+#include <algorithm>
 #include <cassert>
 #include <regex>
 
